.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-completions 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-completions \- Prints a completion script for bash, zsh, fish, or powershell
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring completions\fR [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISHELL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints a completion script for bash, zsh, fish, or powershell
.PP
The script completes commands, flags and values, with context names and agent IDs read from this machine\*(Aqs files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fISHELL\fR>
The shell to print the script for
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
bash: GNU Bash
.IP \(bu 2
zsh: Z shell
.IP \(bu 2
fish: The friendly interactive shell
.IP \(bu 2
powershell: PowerShell, on any platform
.RE
.SH EXTRA
Add the line for your shell to its startup file:

  bash, in ~/.bashrc:
    source <(fleetring completions bash)
  zsh, in ~/.zshrc, after compinit:
    source <(fleetring completions zsh)
  fish, in ~/.config/fish/config.fish:
    fleetring completions fish | source
  PowerShell, in $PROFILE:
    fleetring completions powershell | Out\-String | Invoke\-Expression

The script runs this binary on each Tab, so it follows upgrades.
